```
ROLE: area_chair
FINAL_VERDICT: yellow
REVIEWER_VOTES: {novelty_killer: yellow, systems_reviewer: yellow, evaluation_prosecutor: yellow, theory_skeptic: yellow, product_realist: yellow}
FATAL_OBJECTIONS: []
REQUIRED_EVIDENCE: [
  "L2: real-model maj@k ranking inversion on a symbolic-answer benchmark (MATH/MATH-500) using boxed extractor + numeric/sympy grader, >=2 model pairs with differing answer-surface concentration, k>=32, >=300 problems, multiple seeds with bootstrap CIs",
  "Real-model-sample phi (H_C vs H_W) measured on MATH from actual LLM output frequencies, not proxy surface-form generators — this is the single unmeasured load-bearing quantity",
  "Monotone phi-keyed slope across >=3 recall levels (EXACT / LEXICAL / NUMERIC) to validate the governing-law framing beyond a two-point comparison",
  "Crisp written distinction from Kuhn2023/Farquhar2024 semantic entropy (meaning-clustering for uncertainty vs. sign-flip on plurality accuracy) — novelty_killer flags this as uncomfortably close"
]
MANDATORY_BASELINES: [
  "Wang et al. 2022 — Self-Consistency (the monotonicity assumption this claim negates; direct parent)",
  "Kuhn et al. 2023 / Farquhar et al. 2024 — Semantic Entropy (nearest mechanism neighbor; must explicitly distinguish clustering-for-uncertainty from sign-flip-on-accuracy)",
  "Bulian et al. 2022 — BEM / Tomayto Tomahto (answer-equivalence beyond exact match; foundational premise)",
  "Biderman et al. 2024 — Evaluation Reproducibility (unconditional rank-sensitivity precedent; must distinguish from phi-conditioned law)",
  "Alternative voting rules immune to spoiler effect (Borda/ranked-choice) — evaluation_prosecutor: needed to prove this is a canonicalizer-recall problem, not just a naive plurality problem"
]
MAP_DELTA_PROPOSAL: {node: "CLAIM-0048", change: "status: seed -> yellow-gated-L2; evidence_level: L1-ecological-foothold-validated; gate: L2-real-MATH-inversion-demonstration; add risk_tag: proxy-phi-frequencies, near-tautological-phi-geometry"}
PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: no
RATIONALE: Unanimous 5/5 YELLOW with zero RED and zero GREEN — a rare case where all five independent reviewers converge on the same assessment, which I take as strong signal that the evidence is in a genuinely intermediate state rather than a borderline call.

WHAT IS VALIDATED: The ecological foothold is real. q=1.0000 on 244,864 merged pairs with zero adversarial false-merges proves real numeric/sympy graders are high-precision and the L0 wash-out zone (q<=0.6) does not apply to production-grade canonicalizers. MATH-500 exhibits strong phi<<0 (median -1.0 to -1.2, 86-90% of problems, H_C~1.15 vs H_W~2.0), confirming the recall-HURTS regime has a foothold in real symbolic-answer benchmarks. The Stage-B GSM8K null (no ranking flip, near-identity bucket collapse) is the PREDICTED outcome for phi~0 integer-answer QA, so it CONFIRMS rather than refutes the phi-governance story. The dataset-specific guidance (symbolic-answer evals are at risk, integer-answer evals are not) is an actionable, evidence-backed contribution even without L2.

WHAT IS NOT VALIDATED — AND WHY GREEN IS BLOCKED: (1) The headline claim is that canonicalizer recall can INVERT model rankings. This inversion exists only in L0 simulation, which the packet itself flags as post-hoc-retuned exploratory. The single real-model test (Stage B) produced a null on the wrong regime. A claim whose headline consequence is shown only in simulation cannot be GREEN. (2) The theory_skeptic raises a serious structural concern: MATH phi<<0 may be near-tautological given |correct_support|=1 vs |wrong_support|>=3 under any surface generator — H_C<H_W follows from support-size asymmetry, not from an empirical discovery about LLM behavior. The +0.86->+0.26 GSM8K phi shift under symmetric surface treatment demonstrates generator-tunability. Without real-model-sample phi, the load-bearing quantity is a property of the proxy DGP, not of LLMs. (3) Prior-art search is NOT adequate: novelty_killer explicitly reports that live web search was denied this session, so the required >=2-source fatal-collision verification could not be completed. Per my mandate, I cannot emit GREEN without adequate prior-art search. The semantic-entropy line (Kuhn2023/Farquhar2024) is flagged as uncomfortably close and not yet crisply distinguished. The "when does self-consistency fail" and lm-eval extraction-robustness literatures were not searched. (4) The evaluation_prosecutor correctly identifies a missing mandatory baseline: alternative voting rules (Borda, ranked-choice) that are immune to the spoiler effect — without this, the claim cannot distinguish "canonicalizer-recall is the problem" from "plurality voting is the problem."

WHY NOT RED: No reviewer found a fatal objection. The mechanism is coherent (spoiler/Duverger applied to eval is a legitimate, if narrow, domain-application). The q=1.0 + MATH phi<<0 ecological evidence is real, not fabricated or circular. The GSM8K null is honest and confirmatory. The packet's own disposition (keep-exploring, not claiming validation) is appropriately calibrated. The contribution — even at L1 — provides actionable guidance: teams running maj@k on symbolic-answer benchmarks should be aware that high-recall canonicalizers may hurt accuracy in the phi<<0 regime. That is a useful, evidence-backed finding, even without the dramatic inversion.

ADJUDICATION NOTES: The theory_skeptic's near-tautology concern and the evaluation_prosecutor's alternative-voting-rule baseline are the two sharpest objections. Both are manageable (real-model phi + Borda baseline in L2) but neither is addressed in the current evidence. The novelty_killer's assessment that this is a "domain-application + governing-law refinement" rather than a new mechanism is shared by all reviewers and by the packet itself — this sets the ceiling: even a perfect L2 yields a validated domain-application paper, not a mechanism-discovery paper. That ceiling is acceptable for the eval-and-safety node.

VERDICT: YELLOW — genuine partial result with a clear, specific gate. The ecological foothold is validated; the headline consequence is not. L2 spec is well-defined (REQUIRED_EVIDENCE above). If L2 demonstrates a real-MATH inversion with real-model phi<<0 and the semantic-entropy distinction is written, GREEN becomes defensible. If L2 shows real-model phi~0 on MATH (i.e., real LLMs concentrate errors differently than the proxy assumes), the claim narrows to a theoretical possibility without ecological bite — at which point RED.
```
